able of $f(x,y)$ shown below.\n\n| $y>-1$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=-1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ecbba4555023bdc89892cd902b30039e3a76a919b68c5a2bec670213dfc78c34.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/9ca3f95ecca25c73eadd7cbd3840cbc1f8336ff7a1a1598876c11bd4af16805b.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-{x}^{3}$ | $(y+1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-2)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-2)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/e02c333ffb3063ebf0f214cf88cb9a6d486cff0db958de6d47943f3ca0739e45.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-326436/field-1" "q-326436/field-2" "q-326436/field-3" "q-326436/field-4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-326436"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971/selection/c8a570a7a45299d6bca7534749498af91d95f2281bdd8454030e707cf44ee838" :answer/id #uuid "db6d40c5-e2c0-5946-99d2-7d8f1a508394" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971/selection/bab4acf5ca3a66ed4f11bbcf7574627e6848417923ee89f9393917451c190309" :answer/id #uuid "bc7c0266-869b-5f46-9251-f7d45ad77979" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971/selection/a3c72559d7d25083af41603553dab28f112bf464761c0eb8d3b6e870c70cfb9e" :answer/id #uuid "dd461320-244c-5daa-985d-40605a216206" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971/selection/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" :answer/id #uuid "f5319bce-f88c-581b-a6dd-645e7a59d343" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971/selection/46070df805b4653a5d877039a93fbcfb0cf7186aafc46672fa7e330153961054" :answer/id #uuid "6f3a246c-800f-5999-9b93-b9ed1cd1d295" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0a0b78-80b6-526e-91f3-053687642870" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120971/selection/a3c72559d7d25083af41603553dab28f112bf464761c0eb8d3b6e870c70cfb9e" :answer-field/choices ["q-120971/selection/c8a570a7a45299d6bca7534749498af91d95f2281bdd8454030e707cf44ee838" "q-120971/selection/bab4acf5ca3a66ed4f11bbcf7574627e6848417923ee89f9393917451c190309" "q-120971/selection/a3c72559d7d25083af41603553dab28f112bf464761c0eb8d3b6e870c70cfb9e" "q-120971/selection/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" "q-120971/selection/46070df805b4653a5d877039a93fbcfb0cf7186aafc46672fa7e330153961054"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120971" :question/id #uuid "ffd06503-0d35-5908-aec5-906d9832f7e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-120971" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=(x-2)(y+1)^{2}.$  What are the missing entries in the sign table of $f(x,y),$ shown below?\n\n| $y>-1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=2$ and $y=-1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/a66a57932dbc935b5ed6f74b4f0faa0047c4b7ef58ded46be088dad30fa5eee4.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/52efe97fcffa3da05151b3ffef5305e0c3ec0d567d3f62b964a30740c08a3981.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x-2)$ | $(y+1)^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-2,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(4,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-2,-3)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(4,-3)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/aa100568c18b31507c775e77ed3201a5aed6f708b541e48046617a43fe9a8304.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<2$ | $x>2$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120971/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120971"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553/selection/072defd9f3719dd633eae6d25836446ed83829128643e09b9c5daf49781dfe67" :answer/id #uuid "51cdf062-77d3-53fc-b3a0-4ccd9f0d2e1f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/330f6080a3640f193e3d1650405030c049f059aaa9e3c6f280d2355382ed2e69.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553/selection/58c23c37dfd4317af74eb28b4c4da9dfd2bbd35e78301dbeabfb48071acc245a" :answer/id #uuid "f3c669d3-d855-58be-8f27-56cead888a48" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/02a01c1a57b61374e7f9c44b7609f7c0b48c9f91a44ffd0d4a86afeb0909ed68.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553/selection/e09ce50a3242a586067d1593bb255ddb0ddde6fb333700655f69f026fedc116e" :answer/id #uuid "3da33b3f-5b9a-5853-9477-74cbb9fcc973" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ba2d7fbeb1a79d32f499e3c3ae81595e4a58fdd4486c6e558fc129fe0e5b3385.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553/selection/ec1feb4b15a0dacd6d784d5a24872755ef167f1395f8c606a15427b8ee0648fb" :answer/id #uuid "d533bd23-d1ab-578e-aee5-b52d4c72a90c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/d1958e53fc544743a537eccab139fa33716823e3b57b4aeac90c3b17ec7e8e48.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553/selection/53e6e371124744c10cde3bff1f23789d608e9e82cfd50ea572d807e2f1e6164b" :answer/id #uuid "109d3ab8-3738-54b4-aee0-77f5d905df8f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ff554d3264fe5aeb9cca37a143888c8eb7a7e31f9bcdb3f8512309e45397aeb2.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd4a7138-7632-523f-84fa-1bf20cd8015f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-149553/selection/e09ce50a3242a586067d1593bb255ddb0ddde6fb333700655f69f026fedc116e" :answer-field/choices ["q-149553/selection/072defd9f3719dd633eae6d25836446ed83829128643e09b9c5daf49781dfe67" "q-149553/selection/58c23c37dfd4317af74eb28b4c4da9dfd2bbd35e78301dbeabfb48071acc245a" "q-149553/selection/e09ce50a3242a586067d1593bb255ddb0ddde6fb333700655f69f026fedc116e" "q-149553/selection/ec1feb4b15a0dacd6d784d5a24872755ef167f1395f8c606a15427b8ee0648fb" "q-149553/selection/53e6e371124744c10cde3bff1f23789d608e9e82cfd50ea572d807e2f1e6164b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-149553" :question/id #uuid "cf0f09c4-74cb-5db2-aad0-f5a0e418906f" :question/math-academy-id "q-149553" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=x(2-y).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)>0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/41f10e527834d0767709b965150054a564eaee9c174204381ed94b0e43077fe0.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/994e35e23e56191ef06a155912a326d28d857f236308655265d18d17bb48531b.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $x$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,3)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)>0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/9710358526e0e14fbf7263ba5d1496cdcb2941f9cb32a1d07b2ea37865163ab2.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149553/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-149553"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267/selection/c9449c2ba3f52703ff56661b80509f9c78acc7bb24669937fd8cd378af2c7ca5" :answer/id #uuid "9f3eecb3-fe56-50c1-ab53-06117d38dc74" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/6d3adc17b4cadfbec159597d585375769300959fcb0cb176b0ccbf469bc98f45.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267/selection/8980753bbe327874a5fede86a8bcc1fc38680b70b23cc351bd2d85c09a964357" :answer/id #uuid "5b4d2334-db89-594c-9a9a-53f8136cf3ce" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/1bd9768a14f9cd4a785dab34e16aa3cb580784b91abaaa57728119910e578d80.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267/selection/da717432ca58fc7b0857236b2cb855aaacefe5e86ef2161d3a8d302614850832" :answer/id #uuid "e0267afc-8e85-5938-9eda-d8537c702617" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/9c7bd1818e2315a950dc2de3e84d35f449eb9627803e21e29ceb618e98cff885.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267/selection/8cd36a9fe7de1d654ccbb0972503cb0e6728ca857bffcf28368c02cc8180dca8" :answer/id #uuid "75dbb13b-7173-53e8-9bf2-353598cd1a2b" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/d3783b95073375680613a63e6964020256128ce8452ddad8fb13dddfc3a1a567.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267/selection/d7572efc261ffe0f6ae0dfde86adfcb1a5786939bbe889a49201f6bad9d76a02" :answer/id #uuid "c31a6458-29cf-58f5-852a-bbedd829531d" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/be5f2602a9f1233bb4e5227a42ff29bb8f2c88e13603384d32d64b0355271594.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bec33654-ca92-5956-a798-6700ffd5376a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-121267/selection/d7572efc261ffe0f6ae0dfde86adfcb1a5786939bbe889a49201f6bad9d76a02" :answer-field/choices ["q-121267/selection/c9449c2ba3f52703ff56661b80509f9c78acc7bb24669937fd8cd378af2c7ca5" "q-121267/selection/8980753bbe327874a5fede86a8bcc1fc38680b70b23cc351bd2d85c09a964357" "q-121267/selection/da717432ca58fc7b0857236b2cb855aaacefe5e86ef2161d3a8d302614850832" "q-121267/selection/8cd36a9fe7de1d654ccbb0972503cb0e6728ca857bffcf28368c02cc8180dca8" "q-121267/selection/d7572efc261ffe0f6ae0dfde86adfcb1a5786939bbe889a49201f6bad9d76a02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-121267" :question/id #uuid "079fdbd8-192c-5486-bfcb-d0943d20768e" :question/math-academy-id "q-121267" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(x+2)(y-1).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\le 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-2$ and $y=1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ce8f784a51d18fd9ea97672b6642b643947845e87b0a4d4c7dd291fcb18f50ed.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/c53a92d71b292288e566db12011c13569ebee65e879598e10b6a14e3acd4f189.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+2)$ | $(y-1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-3,2)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(-1,2)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-3,0)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(-1,0)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\le 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/4d65d4c9829b7161152722b7cf6e8605c1cace8078e53430f3480d5d16d74ec4.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-121267/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-121267"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-121275/selection/bf2f78b14cbfe109397af6cf3a903270cf5a1ae87755e8ee3dcaa17028db4586" :answer/id #uuid "7696613a-467d-5f2c-8480-1ac1b4ada008" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/870d9de880f857a1fe66851ae115575955efb12b4cd651279d7494b4cb99d022.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121275/selection/71d9b42d181af0907204b466724808487f1c813f6eb34e7e30cc139307a60e04" :answer/id #uuid "ee89116a-52c8-5866-8cc0-3ee8b75972f0" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/9505947a6ab1ebfca0aedaeec8cde50e8859dfa7bc2b349833c9d26bd849748b.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-121275/selection/90a2327787c28f948b8e01e45f59753ffae2f3cbff5cca4fb890bc29fc834246" :answer/id #uuid "832679bb-ada0-563a-9bf9-7ddd56714444" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/m